    "class_level": 1,
    "class_level_note": "The Magic Gladiator's, class level 1: he has no second class. 'gladiator' is a class bit ahead of his class (tools/cook.py's kClass), so nobody wears it until he is in.",
    "power_note": "As the other 2nd wings: his blows x(132 + plus)%, what reaches him x(75 - 2 a plus)%, defence + 2 a plus, level + 5 a plus; the option wizardry or damage by its kind bit (sim::wingOption).",
    "number_note": "MU's 12/6; ours 12/22, a number this game leaves free (12/6 is the knight's Orb of Lunge here). docs/second-wings.md."
  },
  "drawn_note": "Drawn as MU draws it, in two more layers (2026-10-07, the user: 'wings look not finished'): the second pass, RENDER_BRIGHT | RENDER_CHROME on Chrome02 at (0.8, 0.6, 1) (ZzzObject.cpp:6970-6976), as game/shine.h's kShineDarkness at 0.4 of MU's strength; and the sparks (:9981-10017), a violet flare at each of ten rib bones and a bolt of the thunder sheet out to its partner, in game/wings.cpp (WingLook::sparks), faint as the monster auras. MU's spirit joint back along each bolt is left out.",
  "sheet_dark_note": "Ours (the user, 2026-10-07: 'work on transparency for black parts on wings'): NDEE's own alpha cuts the shards' outlines through a grey gradient that runs to near-black at one end, and MU draws that end solid. Here its alpha is also faded by its brightness -- nothing under luminance 12, full from 70, smoothstep between -- so the black ends of the shards fade out and the violet joints behind them show through. MuMain's sheet is decoded from Data/Item/NDEE.OZT; this is it with that fade multiplied into its alpha.",
